; Tutorial_3_Check_One_Web_Page.inix -- check one web page

[about]
Title=3 - Check One Web Page
Intro=Checking a single web page, and reading the report urlCheck writes for it.
Setup=urlCheck installed, and a web page you want to check.
Homework=Check the home page of a site you use often, and count its violations.

[step]

Say=One want: to know whether a site's home page has accessibility problems, before writing to its owner about them.
Key=

[step]

Say=I open the dialog. The focus is on Source urls.
Key=Alt+Control+Shift+U
Hear=urlCheck dialog
Hear=Source urls edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type the address. The https part is optional; urlCheck adds it.
Key=
Hear=example.org
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I leave Output folder blank, so reports go into the current folder, and I tick View output.
Key=Alt+V
Hear=View output check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter starts the check. Edge opens the page, waits for it to settle, then runs axe-core.
Key=Enter
Hear=Checking example.org
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A short box reports the totals when it is done.
Key=
Hear=1 page checked
Hear=OK button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter closes it, and File Explorer opens on the output folder. There is a subfolder named after the page's title.
Key=Enter
Hear=Example Domain
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter goes into it. Inside are the report, the workbook, the screenshots and the page's own files.
Key=Enter
Hear=report dot h t m
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter on report dot h t m opens the report in the browser.
Key=Enter
Hear=urlCheck report, heading level 1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=It begins with a summary: the page, when it was checked, and how many rules were violated, passed, or could not be decided.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Violations: 3. Passes: 24. Incomplete: 2.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=H moves to the violations, each rule a heading of its own.
Key=H
Hear=Images must have alternate text, heading level 2
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Under each rule: what it means, how serious it is, which WCAG criterion it maps to, and how many elements break it.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Impact: critical. WCAG 1.1.1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Then each element that breaks it, by its place in the page, with the advice axe gives for fixing it.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Fix: give the image an alt attribute
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Incomplete means axe could not decide by itself, such as colour contrast over a picture; those are for a person to check.
Key=

[step]

Say=Passes are listed too, so the report shows what the page does well as well as what it does wrong.
Key=

[step]

Say=Checking the same page again keeps the first report, since its folder exists; Force replacements checks it afresh.
Key=Alt+F
Hear=Force replacements check box, checked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A violation count is a start, not a verdict: walk seven turns these results into a conformance report with the manual tests still to do.
Key=

[step]

Say=Impact comes in four levels, critical, serious, moderate and minor, which is the order to fix things in.
Key=

[step]

Say=Insert plus F6 lists the report's headings, one for each violated rule, a quick table of contents to the problems.
Key=Insert+F6
Hear=Headings list
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Each element is described by its place in the page and a snippet of its code, which is what a developer needs to find it.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=img src logo dot png
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The WCAG number beside each rule is a link to that criterion's explanation, for anyone who wants the why behind the rule.
Key=K
Hear=link, WCAG 1.1.1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A report from before and after a fix, side by side, is the simplest proof that the fix worked.
Key=

[step]

Say=One page, one report, ready to read. The next walk opens the workbook and its screenshots.
Key=
